      "message": "The randomness is important, and is per spec. (at least in theory)\n\nThe idea is that if there is a collision, we don\u0027t want both sides to keep retrying at exactly the same time. From RFCOMM spec:\n\u003e  How the situation is resolved is up to the implementation (e.g., it may retry after a random time, or leave it up to the user to retry\nmanually).\n\nBut making the range configurable sgtm",
